# Started in a folder that has a catmintc in it, pad uses that one: no --catmintc,
# nothing on the PATH. The stand-in here prints the arguments it was given, so
# the panel shows that it was run, and how: the file, then -o and where the
# program goes. (It has no lib folder beside it, so there is no -I.)
# files t.cm=x
# exec catmintc=#!/bin/sh\necho "fake compiler got: $*"\n
# open t.cm
# frames 4
# expect message built t
# expect panel 1 1
# expect panellast fake compiler got: t.cm -o t
1 key f5
